Restrict Copilot debug/proxy/CAPI URL override settings to user (global) scope only.

These advanced debug settings can redirect Copilot network requests to an
attacker-chosen endpoint. Reading them from workspace or folder scope lets a
malicious repository's .vscode/settings.json silently point requests (and the
credentials attached to them) at an attacker-controlled server. This change
marks the override settings as userScopeOnly and reads them exclusively from
the user's global configuration, ignoring workspace/folder values.

Remove when Code-OSS is updated to >= 1.128.1.

